>serial connector on the printer.

The DB25 is TTA2, the DEC423 is TTA3
I assume the printer has a DB25 as well.
Both are Data Terminal Equipment Style/Pinlayout, so a crossover cable
(2-3, 3-2, 7-7) is required.

>                               I've set the printer to the RS232C
>interface with 9600 baud, 8 bits, Xon/Off on.

That's good for a start, but required is only the same baud rate on
printer and VAX. So, after all is working, I would increase it
to the max for sides of the communication (eg. 38400 bps).

>The SYS$LASER queue stalls and then quits so it's not seeing the printer
>at all.

Before setting up the queue, test the communication itself.

eg. SET HOST/DTE TTA3 and communicate directly with the printers postscript
interpreter. Sending a Control-T should give you a printer status
and statusdict/showpage/... commands are then also possible.

And how did you setup the SYS$LASER queue ?

I would also recommend DCPS (>=2.0), because it's included in the VMS license.

