>windows 95/98/2000 network setup and thought that this might compliment
>what I have maybe as a web server.  If this would work what kind of
>software would you suggest?

Windows-NT 4.0 on Alpha requires Alpha versions of Win32 programs.
Only Win16 programs (like must SETUP.EXEs) run directly (emulated).

If you can't find an Alpha version of some Win32 programs (eg. there was
WinWord and Excel but no PowerPoint thus no Office package for Alpha)
then you could run INTEL binaries on the Alpha with the help of a special
emulator/compiler/optimizer called FX!32 from Digital (later Compaq).
It was terminated (like NT Alpha) years ago.

	http://www.support.compaq.com/amt/fx32/index.html

NOTE: FX!32 won't help you with drivers (like printer drivers) or other
non-usermode applications...

