> find alpha-based
> programs to run under NT or can I run plain old windows applications?

Basically, you have to run programs which explicitly say they are for
WindowsNT on Alpha. Or you can try to run programs under FX!32 (x86
transmutator). The latest version was good and let one run just about
any x86 app, but on a 166Mhz Alpha it'll be like running a 486DX2/66Mhz.
Remember, the Mulita was originally designed as a 'thin client' (eg.
fancy terminal).

There's a great repository of native AlphaNT apps at
http://www.alphant.com . Might be worth a look. You should also be able
to find service packs and [most versions?] of FX!32.

Otherwise, ever consider Linux or NetBSD?? :)

