I have inherited a two-node SCSI cluster comprising a pair
of AlphaStation 200 4/166's (yep, they're a bit long in
tooth :-).

The configuration seems a bit odd to me in that one host
is configured at SCSI ID 6 (OK) and the other is at
SCSI ID 3 (very odd!).  Also, whoever configured this
cluster managed put/keep the CDrom at DKA400 (SCSI ID 4)
for both systems...I _believe_ that only one system's
CD is actually on the SCSI bus, but I could easily be
mistaken.

The two systems share an external StorageWorks shelf,
but given the one host at SCSI ID 3 and the CD at ID 4,
two of the external slots are not usable.  Furthermore
I worry that there may be some performance issues given
the unfair arbitration of SCSI.

So...does anyone know how to set/change the host SCSI ID
on an AlphaStation 200?  I didn't _notice_ any console
variable.  I also couldn't see anything _obvious_ on the
motherboard (yep, I did open 'er up and look :-).

Oh, the cluster does function in this configuration...I'm
just trying to tidy things up before putting them back
into regular use.

Thanks, Ken
