According to configure it does (as LP).

> 
> How about card reader/puncher and tape reader/puncher?

Look in [sys0.syscommon.sys$ldr] for most of the device
drivers (*driver.exe).

You can check for some type of support by running a configure
for them in VMS. The configure option is only used to tell you
what CSR's and Vectors your devices are supposed to be at,
but should tell you if the device is supported.

run sys$system:sysgen
SYSGEN> configure
DEVICE> DHV11
DEVICE> CR11
DEVICE> ^Z		<-- Type a control/Z here
Device: CR11	Name: CRA	CSR: 777160	Vector: 230	Support: yes
Device: DHV11	Name: TXA	CSR: 760440*	Vector: 300*	Support: yes
SYSGEN> ^Z

Configure wants the name of the controller, not the device
being controlled. i.e. rqdx3 instead of rd54.




