Alan Greig <a.greig@virgin.net> writes:
> We had a TU78 installed on a  DEC-20 circa 1980 when it first came
> out. I recall we were supplied with an early release of TOPS-20 V5 (?)
> to support both it and the RP07. In later years the drive was upgraded
> to a TU79 and moved to a VAXCluster. Don't know what exactly was
> changed but it was definitely true that a TU78 could be field upgraded
> to a TU79.

I can't imagine why anyone would *want* to upgrade a TU78 to a TU79,
even if it was possible.  The TU79 doesn't have *any* advantages over
the TU78.  AFAIK, the only reason DEC introduced the TU79 was that
Pertec stopped making the drive DEC OEM'd for the TU78.

Since the transport and cabinet were different, the upgrade would
basically be to throw away the TU78 and put a new TU79 in its place.
The TM78 Massbus tape formatter and the cables would be about the only
parts that you'd keep.


