   I'm just about at wit's end here, and am desperate for some advice.
I installed a DECconcentrator 900TH (two MMF MOD-PMD ports installed,
12 fixed TP-PMD ports) in a DEChub 900 backplane, and I can't figure
out how to connect the DEFPA-UA clients to the concentrator. The 900TH
has the "latest" firmware found on the clearVISN 3.1 CD, but I don't
know what firmware is on the DEFPA's.

   I have a dozen or so of the DEFPA-UA's, and have tried three of
them so far in a dual PIII running Win2k. I previously had a DEFPA-AA
installed, and was able to talk to a DECconcentrator 900MX (with six
MMF MOD-PMD ports), but I swapped out the 900MX with a 900TH, and now
I need to make the TP ports work. Anyway, I've tried three of the
DEFPA-UA's, two known-good Cat5 ethernet cables (verified to be good
TP-PMD cables by a Fluke time-domain reflectometer), and three
different ports on the 900TH. The two ethernet cables are between 10m
and 15m in length, and have "field-installed" RJ45 connectors.

   The cables which tested as "good" by the Fluke have pins 1/2 and
7/8 going straight through, which is the standard pinout for an
ethernet cable. For grins, I cut the end off one of the cables and
swapped 1 and 2 and then 7 and 8, but that resulted in a "bad" cable
according to the Fluke, and it still didn't work.

   The symptom is that the LED's don't light up on the concentrator,
and the LED on the DEFPA-UA just blinks, as though a cable is not even
connected.

   The DEChub has been configured through clearVISN, but I don't know
if it's configured properly. There doesn't seem to be anything to
configure, as far as the TP-PMD ports are concerned. The 900TH has the
internal FDDI ports connected to the backplane, connecting to a
DECswitch 900EF. The two MMF MOD-PMD ports on the 900TH are
functioning properly, and the machines with the DEFPA-AA's are able to
talk through the 900TH/900EF.
 
   Windows 2000 doesn't seem to discern the transceiver type on a
DEFPA, so I don't think it knows that there's a copper interface,
rather than an optic interface. At the very least, I couldn't find any
configuration settings in the control panel which made any difference.

   So, I'm thinking there's probably a software/configuration issue,
but I don't know what -- three cards, two cables (both tested good),
and three ports can't all be bad and show the same symptoms, right...?

   Maybe a firmware problem in the DEFPA-UA's? Maybe a configuration
issue in the 900TH?

 
Thanks in advance,
Chris


