The fact the ifconfig on tap0 makes things worse is probably due
to the fact that MOPD is using DecNET rather that IP AFAIK. As for
the trace and the pfWrite problem - It seems there are three mac
addresses involved
-  00:FF:53:5F:4D:D0 (The host side of tap0)
-  ab:0:0:1:0:0 - Since the first byte is odd, a broadcast addr ?
-  0:50:da:1a:13:c3 - The simulator side of the tap0 ?

Try to change pfWrite in common/pf-linux2.c to

int
pfWrite(fd, buf, len)
int fd, len;
u_char *buf;
{

   if (sendto(fd, buf, len, 0, &socklist[fd].sa, sizeof(struct 
sockaddr)) == len)
     return(len);

   if (len < 0)
       fprintf( stderr, "pfWrite():%s\n", strerror( errno));

    return (-1);
}

No that it solves anything, but it could perhaps provide a clue
as to what is happening ...

 
