The replies have all been regarding the pinout of the cables. I have
found a few places which indicate that pins 1/2 and 7/8 are used for
CDDI.

"Evilnet" uses pins 3/6 and 4/5, so the RJ45-based networking
standards all coexist on a Cat5, EIA/TIA 568A cable. There are many
links on this specific topic, but here is one in particular:
http://www.tuxas.net/lazydoc/easyplugs/

And I should have emphasized that I believe the cabling is correct,
because the $1000 Fluke time-domain reflectometer that I'm using can
ring out TP-PMD (aka CDDI), and the meter indicates that both of my
