Yes, the fixed UTP frontpanel ports (3-14) are fixed M, but the ModPMD ports
(1-2) can be configured as A/M/B/S and can be MMF (ANSI or SC), SMF or UTP.

	http://digitalnetworks.net/dr/hubs/repeater/manuals/

	14 M-ports
	 2 A-/B-ports and 12 M-ports
	 1 A-port and 13 M-ports
	 1 B-port and 13 M-ports
	 1 S-port and 13 M-ports

IIRC I had 2 A-/B-ports, 12 front-panel M-ports and 1 backplane M-port
(but I maybe wrong of course)

So, next step is probably looking into the DECconcentrator for status/port
informations (via ClearVISN) or into your NMS (in case you configured SNMP
trapping and the DEFHU sent a trap for the status of the frontpanel ports).

