Basically if you put the big flexwire in (between the DIN41612 grey
connector and the IDC 50pin connector on the drive) you are all set. The
drive will be fixed at SCSI ID 0 though. The smaller flexwire, which is disk
type specific, will drive the activity and fault LEDs and set the SCSI
ID based on which backplane slot the SBB is installed into.

