Nick:

I've got an AS 255/300 and I've found that they're one of the
easiest systems to pull apart and replace components. If you
have a spare drive bay (there are three in the AS 255) you
could install your replacement drive, copy the contents of
the old drive to the new, and then remove the old. Repeat as
often as required.

If you need diagrams and directions, the compaq website still
has information on these systems in the retired workstation
area under Service Guides. It is very useful information.


