There is no BBR bit in Unit Flags that I am aware of. These bits are
defined: (in hex)

     1   compare reads
     2   compare writes
     4   576 byte sectors
    80   removable media
  1000   write protect (software)
  2000   write protect (hardware)

Sequential commands (READ/WRITE/etc) commands/responses do not have
Unit Flag fields.

The BBR routines should only be invoked by a host if

  1)  an end message has the BAD BLOCK REPORTED bit set in the end
      message flags
and 

  2)  the controller requires host based BBR service

The RQDX3 does it's own BBR, so the host should not be attempting to
'help'.  8-)

Jeff Campbell
