I should have been clearer. He can not expand his memory with more 32 MB
DIMMS. The machine has a limit of 2 sets of 64 MB pairs. Each memory
socket pair is mapped on modulo 512 MB centers. The sparse mapping array
is larger the 4GB when the third xxx MB DIMM pair is installed.

The 32 MB DIMMs must be replaced to expand the memory.

