Hello folks:

I found a bug in rq.c file that cause Ultrix to crash when attempt to find
disk drives to display for system disk selection (finder -r).  I fixed
a bug and Ultrix installation finally asked me to select which system
disk to being restored.  I did that, system disk was restored successfully
and asked me to reboot system.  I did rebooted system and was asked to
select options to install.  I selected all options to install.  It is
processing in progress while I am writing this...  Whew!

I looked into Ultrix sources and learned something from mscp_defs.h.  It 
said that must set UF_RPL bit (0x8000) to set up own BBR work area in
controller side.  RZ and RA disks were not defined with UF_RPL.  I put
it on all RZ and RA disk table.  All problems disappeared.  No,
my RQDX3 emulation does not use BBR work area but set all drives with
UF_RPL bit in unit flags and CF_RPL in controller flag.

Thank you for your help!

-- Tim Stark 

