SNIP

> >
> Hello Adam,
>
> Thank you very much for your help.
>
> I checked if there are duplicate UIDs in the passwd but I found none.
> Then I looked for files in /etc. I found passwd.pag and passwd.dir.
> man passwd leaded me to a command 'vipw'
> man vipw
> told me that this programm creates or recreates  the hashed
> passwd-database (Unfortunately I did not understand it completely).
> I executed 'vipw' , did nothing, but quit ':q'
> and all my problems are solved: Deleted user cannot login to the
> system and all user rights and permissions are correct.
>
> The only thing is, that I do not understand what's going on ...
>
The hashed password database (/etc/passwd.dir and /etc/passwd.pag) were
out of sync with /etc/passwd.
After you used vipw it re-ran the mkpasswd command to recreate the
hashed password database from the password file.
You could also have fixed it by manually running mkpasswd or by removing
/etc/passwd.dir and /etc/passwd.pag
Hope this helps
Adam




